# UI

Login (`features/auth/pages/LoginPage.tsx`) is the **primary visual reference**. Future screens should feel like the same modern, minimal, premium SaaS/AI product.

Placement: `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc`.

## Design language

Prefer:

- Persian RTL, Vazirmatn
- clean typography and strong hierarchy
- generous whitespace
- soft surfaces, subtle borders, subtle shadows
- restrained semantic color
- responsive layouts
- accessible UI
- center-aligned textual content where Login / NotFound / error fallback do

Login bar today: open layout (no card), `max-w-md`, `text-2xl` titles, `text-sm` muted body, borderless `bg-surface` fields, `shadow-none` buttons, semantic tokens only.

Avoid:

- generic dashboard templates
- excessive cards or rounded containers
- heavy borders or shadows
- large decorative gradients
- glassmorphism
- noisy backgrounds
- excessive colors
- giant headings
- template-looking shadcn compositions
- unnecessary decoration / over-engineered effects

Style with Tailwind v4 utilities mapped to `src/index.css`. No hard-coded hex/palette colors. No second CSS framework. No hardcoded BFF URL.

## Loading UI

`LoadingPage` is the Suspense fallback: minimal centered spinner, `PageFrame`, `motion-reduce:animate-none`, `role="status"`. Keep it simple.

## Motion

Subtle, purposeful, short. Prefer CSS/Tailwind. Do not add an animation library for a simple spinner or entrance.

Allowed examples already in the project: `login-enter`, `flow-path`, `animate-spin`, hover/focus/press, theme class change.

Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (`motion-reduce`, and CSS disables `flow-path` / `login-enter`).

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML, keyboard access, visible focus
- Labels; form errors with `aria-invalid` / `aria-describedby` / `role="alert"`
- One `h1` per screen; token contrast
- Real buttons and links
- Reduced-motion support
- ARIA only when native HTML is insufficient
